# Level 1's waves as the original spawns them: every call of the level's
# wave handler ($4FD94) and scenery handler ($4FB42) logged with the frame
# ($CDC), the world line ($CD0), the record (a1) and its kind (d0); every
# enemy destroyed ($6250: the object, its type and position), every whole
# wave cleared (the cash drop, $62AC), every capsule shot ($3EEC) and
# token or cash taken ($4F7C). The ship cannot die or touch the scenery and
# the shop is skipped, as in level-run.exp; fire is held so the ship shoots.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage waves-run-start.ini
stage waves-wave.ini
stage waves-scen.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage waves-clear.ini
stage waves-capsule.ini
stage waves-take.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here, outside any hit, then clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/waves-run-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 2
fire
